=========================================================================
CRITERION 5 — the field doc states the signed contract and the range precondition
=========================================================================
PASS. internal/models/dashboard.go, quoted verbatim:

  Signed contract (lines 101-108):
    101  // in-range days represent) minus that month's actual outflow spend,
    102  // SIGNED (CB1): spend is the negated net of the month's non-excluded
    103  // outflow bucket, not its absolute value. An ordinary month nets
    104  // outflow-negative so this is positive spend, same as before; a
    105  // REFUND-DOMINANT month — one whose outflow-typed rows net POSITIVE,
    106  // e.g. a cruise refund exceeding the month's spending — therefore
    107  // enters the walk as a CREDIT (the balance rises by accrual PLUS the
    108  // net refund), never charged as spend.

  Range-nets-negative precondition on the invariant (lines 120-129):
    120  // Invariant: the last element equals -CombinedCumulativeDelta, up to
    121  // float64 summation noise (not month-rounding slack) — the per-month
    122  // accruals partition the range's days exactly, and the signed per-month
    123  // spends (a refund-dominant month contributes a negative spend, i.e. a
    124  // credit) partition TotalExpenses exactly under the precondition above
    125  // AND the further precondition that the RANGE as a whole still nets
    126  // outflow-negative — TotalExpenses is math.Abs of the whole range's net
    127  // (unchanged by CB1), so a wholly refund-dominant RANGE (the range's own
    128  // outflows net positive) is out of scope: the invariant is not
    129  // guaranteed to hold in that case.

  Both site comments were also updated (verified in the diff): metrics.go
  ~529-537 and ~562-578 (spend site), handlers.go ~1084-1098 (spend site), and
  both cross-reference the other surface.

